WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:08.200
KL swaps pairs; FM moves one node at a time.

2
00:00:08.200 --> 00:00:13.000
So the side sizes change, and a balance window limits them.

3
00:00:13.000 --> 00:00:19.356
Here maxDiff = 1: five nodes split 2 : 3 or 3 : 2.

4
00:00:19.756 --> 00:00:25.444
On seed AE | BCD, A and E have the largest gain: +6.

5
00:00:25.444 --> 00:00:30.022
But moving either one leaves 1 : 4: not legal.

6
00:00:30.022 --> 00:00:33.933
Among the legal candidates, D is largest: +3.

7
00:00:34.333 --> 00:00:37.356
A gain splits into two parts.

8
00:00:37.356 --> 00:00:44.378
FS: D is D–E's only end on its side; after the move it is no longer cut, +5.

9
00:00:44.378 --> 00:00:50.733
TE: C–D has no end on the left; after the move it becomes cut, −2.

10
00:00:50.733 --> 00:00:55.333
Gain 3; for plain edges, that is external minus internal.

11
00:00:55.733 --> 00:01:01.644
Step 1 moves D, cut 9; the left has 3, and A becomes legal.

12
00:01:01.644 --> 00:01:05.778
Step 2 moves A, +6, cut 3.

13
00:01:05.778 --> 00:01:10.578
Then C, E, B all lose, and are tried anyway.

14
00:01:10.578 --> 00:01:13.600
The trials end at cut 12.

15
00:01:14.000 --> 00:01:18.133
Cumulative gains: 3, 9, 7, 1, 0.

16
00:01:18.133 --> 00:01:23.822
The best prefix is k = 2: from the start do only D and A, cut 3.

17
00:01:23.822 --> 00:01:28.289
Pass 2 has no positive prefix, and the algorithm stops.

18
00:01:28.689 --> 00:01:30.822
Four things to keep.

19
00:01:30.822 --> 00:01:36.067
Single moves inside the window; legal first, then largest;

20
00:01:36.067 --> 00:01:41.978
gain = FS − TE; try losses too, accept only the best prefix.

21
00:01:41.978 --> 00:01:46.778
In the lab below, see which moves the balance blocks.
